  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Uppala Ramesh vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 18 January, 2021 Author: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Bench: Cheekati Manavendranath Roy The Hon'Ble Sri Justice Cheekati Manavendranath Roy Criminal Petition Nos. 133, 146, 149 and 158 of 2021 Common Order:",
    "facts": "The record reveals that a case in Crime No.238 of 2020 of Nekarekal Police Station, Guntur District, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272 and 273 r/w Section 34 IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"F.S.S. Act\") was registered against the petitioners in Crl.P.No.133 of 2021; a case in Crime No.513 of 2020 of Atmakur(Kur) Police Station, Kurnool District, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 273 r/w 34 IPC and Section 59(i) of the F.S.S. Act was registered against the petitioners in Crl.P.No.146 of 2021; a case in Crime No.326 of 2020 of Eluru I Town Police Station, West Godavari District, for the offences punishable under Sections 270 and 273 IPC, Section 22 of the Cigarettes and Other Tobacco Products (Prohibition of Advertisement and Regulation of Trade and Commerce, Production, Supply and Distribution) Act, 2003 (for short \"COTP Act\") and Sections 58(1), 26(2)(iv) of the F.S.S. Act was registered against the petitioner in Crl.P.No.149 of 2021; a case in Crime No. 325 of 2020 of Eluru I Town Police Station, West Godavari District, for the offences punishable under Sections 270 and 273 IPC, Section 22 of the COTP Act and Sections 58(1), 26(2)(iv) of the F.S.S. Act was registered against the petitioner in Crl.P.No.158 of 2021 respectively. 4. The petitioners sought quash of the said F.I.Rs registered against them under Section 482 Cr.P.C before this Court.",
    "arguments": "P.C. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor also fairly concedes that the F.I.Rs registered against these petitioners are [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court in the petitions filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C. Uppala Ramesh vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 18 January, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/197059752/ 1 5.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "P.C. Learned Additional Public Prosecutor also fairly concedes that the F.I.Rs registered against these petitioners are [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court in the petitions filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C. Uppala Ramesh vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 18 January, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/197059752/ 1 5.",
